     1	# Provider-Pack Architecture — sdd-dispatch v2 design
     2	
     3	Date: 2026-07-22
     4	Status: approved-in-brainstorm, pending spec review
     5	Target version: 1.2.0
     6	
     7	## Problem
     8	
     9	Provider knowledge (dispatch incantations, gotchas, model inventories, verification
    10	history) for codex / opencode / agy is interleaved across shared reference files:
    11	`dispatch-reference.md` holds all three CLIs, `model-catalog.md` mixes the cross-provider
    12	policy grid with per-provider inventories, and `verification-log.md` is one chronological
    13	stream. This blocks three goals:
    14	
    15	1. **Extensibility** — adding a provider means editing every shared file.
    16	2. **Machine-local relevance** — a machine without (say) agy still drags agy content
    17	   through every skill run; nothing skips absent providers.
    18	3. **Shareability** — there is no self-contained unit another user can take for "just
    19	   the opencode knowledge".
    20	
    21	## Decisions (brainstorm outcomes)
    22	
    23	| Fork | Decision |
    24	| --- | --- |
    25	| Unit of split | **Provider packs inside this plugin** (`providers/<name>/`); core stays shared. Not plugin-per-provider. |
    26	| Availability | **Runtime detection** (`command -v` per pack) **+ optional gitignored override** `providers.local.json`. |
    27	| Policy table | **Core defines roles→tiers (abstract); each pack maps tiers→models.** Adding a provider touches zero core files. |
    28	
    29	## Layout
    30	
    31	```
    32	sdd-dispatch-plugin/
    33	  core/
    34	    roles.md                  # SDD role → required tier + judgment bar (provider-free)
    35	    liveness.md               # self-reaping wrapper, effort-scaled thresholds, resume doctrine
    36	    safety-doctrine.md        # hard gate, controller commits, clean-tree/diff, read-only intent
    37	    playbook.md               # dispatch flavours & economics, E-rules (from sdd-external-dispatch.md)
    38	    verification-protocol.md  # probe suite P1–P12 + reviewer known-defect benchmark
    39	    verification-log.md       # cross-provider incidents and synthesis entries ONLY
    40	  providers/
    41	    codex/    pack.md  models.md  verification-log.md
    42	    opencode/ pack.md  models.md  verification-log.md
    43	    agy/      pack.md  models.md  verification-log.md
    44	  contracts/                  # implementer + task-reviewer contracts (unchanged, provider-agnostic)
    45	  skills/
    46	    sdd/                      # process skeleton + detection + pack resolution
    47	    sdd-dispatch-verify/      # pack-scoped verification
    48	  providers.local.json        # OPTIONAL, gitignored, machine-local
    49	```
    50	
    51	## The pack contract
    52	
    53	A directory under `providers/` is a valid pack iff it contains:
    54	
    55	### `pack.md`
    56	Starts with a YAML front-matter block — the machine-readable interface:
    57	
    58	```yaml
    59	---
    60	name: opencode
    61	cli: opencode                     # binary name
    62	detect: command -v opencode       # availability probe (exit 0 = present)
    63	version-probe: opencode --version
    64	resume: opencode run -s <session-id>   # continuation incantation (+ --fork variant note)
    65	session-source: opencode session list  # where session ids come from
    66	stall-signal: log-age             # log-age | process+print-timeout
    67	sandbox: none                     # enforced | none
    68	---
    69	```
    70	
    71	Body (prose, version-stamped): dispatch template, verified behavior, gotchas, auth notes,
    72	output conventions. All content that today lives in that provider's section of
    73	`dispatch-reference.md`.
    74	
    75	### `models.md`
    76	Tier→model table for this provider:
    77	
    78	| Tier | Lane | Priority | Model id | Status | Pricing | Rationale |
    79	| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    80	| cheapest | any | 1 | … | verified/listed/rejected | … | … |
    81	| standard | implement | 1 | … | | | |
    82	| standard | review | 1 | … | | | |
    83	| most-capable | any | 1 | … | | | |
    84	
    85	**Lane** (`implement` | `review` | `any`, default `any`) exists because a tier alone can
    86	under-specify: a provider may field different same-tier models for implementing vs
    87	reviewing (opencode: minimax-m3 implements at standard, deepseek-v4-pro reviews at
    88	standard). Resolution matches (tier, lane) with `any` as wildcard; the one-priority-1
    89	rule applies per (tier, lane) pair.
    90	
    91	A tier MAY list alternates: multiple rows per tier, ordered by an explicit **Priority**
    92	column (1 = default; ascending = fallback order when the default is unavailable,
    93	rejected, or has just failed a task in this session). Row order in the file carries no
    94	meaning — only Priority does. Rows with Status `rejected` are never resolved regardless
    95	of priority (they remain in the table as documented evidence). Duplicate priorities
    96	within a tier are a pack validity error. Example: opencode adaptation tier —
    97	minimax-m3 priority 1, qwen3.7-plus priority 2.
    98	Plus watch list and rejected-models section (with evidence links into the pack's log).
    99	Namespaces, free-tier caveats, and per-model warnings (e.g. Luna long-context recall)
   100	live here.
   101	
   102	### `verification-log.md`
   103	Append-only, this provider's probes, incidents, and model evaluations. Never rewritten.
   104	
   105	**Extensibility rule:** a new provider = one new directory following this contract.
   106	No core file changes. Sharing = copy the directory (or PR it upstream).
   107	
   108	## Core contents
   109	
   110	- **`roles.md`** — the abstract policy, provider-free:
   111	
   112	  | SDD role | Tier | Mode |
   113	  | --- | --- | --- |
   114	  | Transcription implementer (complete code in brief) | cheapest | bg, write |
   115	  | Adaptation implementer (prose/design/debug) | standard | bg, write |
   116	  | Large-codebase / long-context implement | most-capable | bg, write |
   117	  | Read-only explore | cheapest | bg, read-only* |
   118	  | Research / synthesis | standard | bg, read-only* |
   119	  | Per-task reviewer | standard | bg, read-only* |
   120	  | Final whole-branch / design review | most-capable | bg, read-only* |
   121	
   122	  Plus the tiering rules (turn count beats token price; scale reviewer to diff;
   123	  read-only is intent except where a pack declares `sandbox: enforced`).
   124	- **`liveness.md`** — self-reaping wrapper template, effort-scaled thresholds
   125	  (300s low/med, 600–900s high/xhigh), the `stall-signal` dispatch on pack front-matter
   126	  (agy-style buffering CLIs are watched by process + print-timeout, never log age),
   127	  kill-is-checkpoint recovery, pid-only kills, evidence-first "is it running" rules.
   128	- **`safety-doctrine.md`** — hard gate, controller commits, clean-tree-before/diff-after
   129	  on `sandbox: none` packs, never-trust-self-report.
   130	- **`playbook.md`** — dispatch flavours (inline / sub / ext / supervised) & economics,
   131	  token-efficiency rules E1–E7, triviality floor, batching.
   132	- **`verification-protocol.md`** — probe suite P1–P12, plus (new, promoted from smoke
   133	  run 2) the **reviewer known-defect benchmark**: re-run a candidate reviewer on a diff
   134	  where a trusted model already caught a defect; a false-clean fails the candidate.
   135	- **`verification-log.md`** — cross-provider synthesis and incidents spanning providers
   136	  (e.g. the harness wrapper-notification findings). Per-provider events go to pack logs.
   137	
   138	## Detection & resolution flow (skill Step 0)
   139	
   140	1. For each `providers/*/pack.md`, run its `detect:` command → **detected set**.
   141	2. If `providers.local.json` exists, apply it:
   142	   ```json
   143	   { "disable": ["codex"], "prefer": "opencode", "note": "no ChatGPT seat on this box" }
   144	   ```
   145	   `disable` removes detected providers; `prefer` sets the default lane when the plan
   146	   doesn't name one. → **active set**.
   147	3. Load ONLY active packs' `pack.md` + `models.md`.
   148	4. Role→model resolution: role → tier (core `roles.md`) → model (active pack's
   149	   `models.md`), honoring the session's routing lever.
   150	5. If the plan/lever names an **inactive** provider: surface to the user (named provider
   151	   is absent/disabled here — reroute or abort?). Never silently reroute.
   152	
   153	`providers.local.json` is machine policy, not capability: it can only disable/steer, never
   154	enable an undetected CLI.
   155	
   156	## Skill changes
   157	
   158	- **`skills/sdd/SKILL.md`** — keeps the process skeleton (Step 0, dispatch overrides,
   159	  flavour choice, controller rules) but references `core/*` and "the active packs";
   160	  the per-CLI gotcha quick-list moves into pack.md bodies; Step 0 gains the
   161	  detection/resolution steps above.
   162	- **`skills/sdd-dispatch-verify/SKILL.md`** — becomes pack-scoped: verify one named
   163	  provider (only its pack files + log change) or sweep the active set. Model evaluations
   164	  use the known-defect reviewer benchmark + small implementer probe as standard.
   165	  Version bump policy unchanged (patch per verification commit).
   166	
   167	## Migration plan (content re-org, zero information loss)
   168	
   169	1. Create `core/` and `providers/{codex,opencode,agy}/`; move every fact from the five
   170	   current reference files into exactly one new home (mapping table kept in the
   171	   migration commit message).
   172	2. Split `verification-log.md`: cross-provider narratives stay in core; per-provider
   173	   entries copied into pack logs (originals preserved — logs are append-only history).
   174	3. Replace the five old files with one-line tombstones ("moved to core/… or
   175	   providers/…") for one release, since installed skill caches may reference old paths.
   176	4. Update both SKILL.md files, README, and `.gitignore` (+`providers.local.json`).
   177	5. Version → **1.2.0**; reinstall/reload; memory file pointer updated.
   178	
   179	## Testing
   180	
   181	1. **Detection**: dry Step-0 run on this machine → all three packs active; with
   182	   `providers.local.json` disabling codex → codex skipped and lever "via codex"
   183	   surfaces a user question.
   184	2. **Resolution**: one tiny ext-dispatch resolving role→tier→model purely through the
   185	   new pack files (no old paths anywhere in the skill run).
   186	3. **Pack validity**: front-matter of each pack parses; `detect`/`version-probe`
   187	   commands run clean; every tier in `models.md` has exactly one priority-1 row and no
   188	   duplicate priorities; no `rejected` row is resolvable.
   189	4. **Tombstones**: grep the repo for references to the five old paths — only tombstones
   190	   remain.
   191	
   192	## Out of scope (backlog)
   193	
   194	- Extracting packs into standalone marketplace plugins (layout deliberately preserves
   195	  this as a future move).
   196	- Auto-generated cross-provider comparison grid rendered from pack `models.md` files
   197	  (rejected for now: generated artifacts drift; revisit if eyeballing lanes side-by-side
   198	  is missed in practice).
   199	- A `pack.md` JSON-schema validator script in the verify skill.

