   173	## opencode (verified v1.17.18, 2026-07-22)
   174	
   175	### Dispatch
   176	```bash
   177	# prompt is POSITIONAL — `-p` is basic-auth password, not prompt
   178	opencode run --auto -m <provider/model> --variant <high|max|minimal…> \
   179	  --dir <repo> "Read <brief-file> …"
   180	```
   181	
   182	### Verified behavior
   183	- **No sandbox**: with no permission config present, headless `opencode run` read files,
   184	  wrote files, and executed shell commands **without `--auto`**. `--auto`
   185	  ("auto-approve permissions not explicitly denied") only matters once a permission config
   186	  exists — keep passing it as intent documentation.
   187	- **`-p` means password** (basic auth for `--attach` mode). Carrying the agy `-p "<PROMPT>"`
   188	  habit over silently misfires. The prompt is a positional argument.
   189	- **No stdin hang** (verified under timeout with open stdin) — `< /dev/null` optional.
   190	- `--variant` sets provider-specific reasoning effort — but is **silently ignored** when
   191	  unsupported or misspelled (`--variant bogusvariant` ran without complaint). Never assume
   192	  it took effect.
   193	- Exit codes normal: 0 success; bogus model → JSON error (`"ref": "err_…"`), exit 1.
   194	- Useful extras seen in `run --help`: `--format json` (raw JSON events), `-f/--file`
   195	  attachments, `-s/--session` + `--fork` continuation, `--attach` to a running server.
   196	- Model namespace: `opencode/<model>` and `opencode-go/<model>` are distinct lists —
   197	  e.g. `deepseek-v4-flash-free` and `gemini-3.5-flash-lite` exist **only** under `opencode/`.
   198	- **Intermittent zero-output startup hang (observed 2026-07-22, v1.17.18/Zen):**
   199	  backgrounded `opencode run` occasionally hangs before its first output byte — process
   200	  alive, log 0 bytes indefinitely; hit resume (`-s`), `--fork`, and cold dispatches alike
   201	  (~5× in one window) while every foreground run succeeded. Cause undetermined (suspect
   202	  non-tty/piped stdio at startup). Handling: 0-byte log past the 5-min threshold = stall →
   203	  kill (by pid), retry once; second consecutive stall → switch to a FOREGROUND dispatch
   204	  (short tasks) or apply a sub-2k fix inline. Exit codes are useless here — judge by log
   205	  bytes only.
   206	- **Session ids are NOT in plain-text run logs** — get them from `opencode session list`
   207	  (newest first) for `-s` resume/`--fork`.
