    59	## 2026-07-22 — incident notes from first live /sdd run (smoke test)
    60	
    61	- **Stdin-hang gotcha fired in production shape**: a Task-2 dispatch composed inside a
    62	  compound command omitted `< /dev/null` → codex hung with the documented signature
    63	  ("Reading additional input from stdin…", log frozen at 39 bytes). Caught by the
    64	  evidence-first liveness check (triggered by the user asking "is it still running?"),
    65	  killed, re-dispatched with the redirect — clean DONE. The redirect is easy to drop when
    66	  the dispatch is embedded in a larger shell line: putting it LAST after the redirections
    67	  is the safe habit.
    68	- **pgrep self-match false-alive**: `pgrep -f 'codex exec'` matches the checking shell's
    69	  own command string and unrelated `codex app-server` daemons; a naive `pkill` then kills
    70	  the checker itself. Fixed pattern: bracket the first letter (`'[b]in/codex exec'`).
    71	  dispatch-reference liveness section updated.
    72	- Full pipeline otherwise green end-to-end: contract compliance (no implementer commits,
    73	  ≤15-line status blocks), enforced read-only reviewer, two-verdict reviews with
    74	  file:line evidence, controller gate + commits, ledger, Sol final review READY TO MERGE.
