     1	# SDD Dispatch Verification Protocol
     2	
     3	The repeatable probe suite for (re)verifying dispatch-CLI behavior. Run it per CLI when a
     4	trigger fires (see README.md), then append results to [verification-log.md](verification-log.md)
     5	and update [dispatch-reference.md](dispatch-reference.md) / [model-catalog.md](model-catalog.md).
     6	
     7	The invocable form of this process is this plugin's `sdd-dispatch-verify` skill
     8	(`${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/sdd-dispatch-verify/SKILL.md`).
     9	
    10	## Ground rules
    11	
    12	- **Work in a scratchpad directory**, never a real repo. Clean up all artifacts afterward.
    13	- **Never mask exit codes with pipes.** `cmd | head; echo $?` reports `head`'s exit code —
    14	  use `cmd > out.txt 2>&1; echo $?` or `${PIPESTATUS[0]}`.
    15	- Capture the **version first**; every recorded fact is version-stamped.
    16	- Confirm side effects **on disk** (`ls`, `cat`), never from the agent's prose.
    17	- Bound every probe with a `timeout` — hang detection is a first-class result
    18	  (exit 124/143 = hung).
    19	- A refuted prior fact is recorded as a refutation, not silently overwritten.
    20	
    21	## Probe suite
    22	
    23	Run per CLI. `$SCRATCH` = a session scratchpad dir.
    24	
    25	### P1 — Version & surface
    26	```bash
    27	which <cli>; <cli> --version
    28	<cli> <run-subcommand> --help        # diff flags against dispatch-reference.md
    29	<cli> models                          # where supported; diff against model-catalog.md
    30	```
    31	
    32	### P2 — Trivial dispatch + exit code (success path)
    33	Prompt: `Reply with exactly the word PONG and nothing else. Do not use any tools.`
    34	Expect: PONG on stdout, exit 0. Record any banner noise around it.
    35	
    36	### P3 — Bogus model (error path + validation)
    37	Dispatch with `-m totally-bogus-model-xyz` (unpiped, capture raw `$?`).
    38	Expect: clean error + nonzero exit. Record whether validation is client- or server-side
    39	and whether the error lists valid models.
    40	
    41	### P4 — Stdin hang
    42	Run P2's command **without** `< /dev/null`, fed from a never-closing pipe, under `timeout 60`:
    43	```bash
    44	tail -f /dev/null | timeout 60 <cli> <dispatch…> "Reply STDINTEST"
    45	```
    46	Exit 124/143 ⇒ hangs (redirect mandatory). Completion ⇒ redirect optional.
    47	
    48	### P5 — Read permission (no flags)
    49	Seed `$SCRATCH/readtest.txt` with a sentinel (`the secret word is XYZZY42`), dispatch
    50	**without any permission flags**: `Read the file readtest.txt and tell me the secret word.`
    51	Record whether the read succeeded, was denied, or hung waiting for approval.
    52	
    53	### P6 — Write permission (no flags, then with flags)
    54	Dispatch without permission flags: `Create a file named writetest.txt containing exactly HELLO.`
    55	Verify **on disk**. If denied, repeat with the CLI's permission flags and record the minimum
    56	flag set that permits writes.
    57	
    58	### P7 — Sandbox escape (only if a sandbox is claimed)
    59	Ask the agent to write **inside** the workspace, to **/tmp**, and to **$HOME** in one task,
    60	reporting per-path results. Verify each on disk. Records the sandbox's true boundary.
    61	
    62	### P8 — Git commit inside sandbox
    63	`git init` a throwaway repo in `$SCRATCH`, seed one commit, then dispatch:
    64	`Create gitfile.txt, git add it, git commit with message 'test commit'. Report any git errors verbatim.`
    65	Verify with `git log`. Records whether `.git` is writable (controller-commits rationale).
    66	
    67	### P9 — Reasoning-effort knob
    68	Dispatch with the CLI's effort mechanism at a valid value, then with a **bogus** value.
    69	Record: accepted / errored / **silently ignored** (the dangerous case), and any
    70	constraints (e.g. agy: `--effort` errors when combined with an effort-suffixed model name).
    71	
    72	### P10 — Output contract / artifact diversion
    73	Dispatch a document-shaped task: `Produce a well-structured 500-word design document titled '<X>' covering …`
    74	Compare stdout size vs. content. If stdout is banner-only, hunt for the artifact
    75	(agy: `find ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain -name '*.md' -mmin -10 -not -path '*/.system_generated/*'`).
    76	Also verify any report-file flag (codex `-o`): does it hold the full transcript or last message only?
    77	
    78	### P11 — Argument-parsing footguns
    79	Probe known traps and candidates from `--help` diffs:
    80	- agy: flag placed immediately after `-p` (does it become the prompt? is the model dropped?)
    81	- opencode: `-p` collision (password vs prompt habit)
    82	- any new short-flag ambiguities the help text suggests
    83	
    84	### P12 — New-model dispatch check
    85	For each model newly present in P1's list: one P2-style probe to confirm it actually
    86	dispatches (catalog "listed" → "verified"). For each model in the catalog now *absent*:
    87	record the removal.
    88	
    89	## Recording
    90	
    91	Append to [verification-log.md](verification-log.md):
    92	
    93	```markdown
    94	## YYYY-MM-DD — <cli> <version> (trigger: <version bump | model release | anomaly | quarterly>)
    95	
    96	| Probe | Assertion under test | Verdict | Evidence |
    97	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
    98	| P4 | `< /dev/null` mandatory | Confirmed | hung 60s, exit 143, "Reading additional input…" |
    99	| …  | | Confirmed / Refuted / Refined / New | one-line raw evidence |
   100	```
   101	
   102	Then:
   103	1. Update dispatch-reference.md (facts + version stamps) and model-catalog.md (inventory, watch list).
   104	2. If findings change how the `sdd` skill should dispatch, update `skills/sdd/SKILL.md`
   105	   and `contracts/` in the same round.
   106	3. Clean up `$SCRATCH` artifacts (including throwaway git repos and any `/tmp` escapes from P7).
   107	4. Commit in the plugin repo; bump the plugin version for behavior-fact changes.
