   138	## codex (verified v0.144.3, 2026-07-22)
   139	
   140	### Dispatch
   141	```bash
   142	codex exec -m <model> -C <repo> -s workspace-write -c approval_policy="never" \
   143	  -c model_reasoning_effort=<low|medium|high|max> \
   144	  --add-dir <parent-dir-for-cross-repo> --skip-git-repo-check \
   145	  -o <report-file> "Read <brief-file> — your complete requirements. … Begin." < /dev/null
   146	```
   147	
   148	### Verified behavior
   149	- **Stdin**: with a piped/open stdin, codex prints `Reading additional input from stdin...`
   150	  and reads to EOF, appending stdin to the prompt. An unclosed pipe hangs it forever →
   151	  `< /dev/null` is mandatory.
   152	- **Sandbox is real**: a write to `~/` fails with "read-only file system". Two carve-outs:
   153	  - `/tmp` **is writable by design** — don't treat the sandbox as total containment, and
   154	    don't let agents stage artifacts there that you'll forget to clean.
   155	  - **`.git` is read-only by design, not intermittently**: working-tree writes succeed while
   156	    `git commit` deterministically fails on `.git/index.lock`. Controller-commits is
   157	    structural, not a flakiness workaround.
   158	- `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` is blocked by the Claude Code auto-mode
   159	  permission classifier — `workspace-write` + `approval_policy="never"` is the working ceiling.
   160	- **`-s read-only` exists and makes codex the only CLI with an *enforced* read-only
   161	  dispatch** — use it for all reviewer roles (the tier table's "read-only" mode is intent
   162	  on agy/opencode but enforcement here).
   163	- `-o <file>` contains **only the agent's final message** — verify via `git diff` + your own
   164	  gate re-run, never the report prose.
   165	- Model IDs and `model_reasoning_effort` are **server-validated**: bogus values → HTTP 400,
   166	  exit 1, with a clear JSON error.
   167	- Model IDs verified dispatching: `gpt-5.6-luna`, `gpt-5.6-terra`, `gpt-5.6-sol`.
   168	- Known model quirk: **Luna long-context recall ~41%** (Sol/Terra ~90%) — bump Luna→Terra
   169	  the moment a task reasons over a large codebase/diff.
